 \begin{abstract}
-Fallback recovery depends on both candidate acquisition and acceptance. We isolate these decisions using a text-compression trigger and fixed four-feature selector. On 7,500 frozen Common Voice recordings, selective recovery lowers macro word error rate by 2.26 percentage points and matches unconditional recovery's error counts in all three seeds. Development-exposed CV27 TEST retains 99.98\% of pooled positive edit gain. Matched-bank unweighted ranking trails expected risk in every seed; Direct's and edit-weighted ranking's advantages concentrate in individual checkpoints and depend on source. Three-checkpoint stratified timing estimates show up to 5.15\% savings over unconditional reranked recovery; Native remains faster. Code: \url{https://github.com/Zhifan-Pan/ISCAS2027}.
+Fallback recovery depends on both candidate acquisition and acceptance. We separate these decisions using a text-compression trigger and fixed four-feature selector. On 7,500 frozen Common Voice recordings, selective recovery lowers macro word error rate by 2.26 percentage points and matches unconditional recovery's error counts in every seed. Retrospective CV27 TEST comparisons retain 99.98\% of positive edit gain. On matched banks, unweighted ranking trails expected-risk training across seeds, whereas advantages from direct adoption and edit-gap weighting depend on source and checkpoint. Timing across three checkpoints estimates up to 5.15\% savings over unconditional reranked recovery, although Native remains faster. Code is available at \url{https://github.com/Zhifan-Pan/ISCAS2027}.
 \end{abstract}
